[Music]  marvel's moon knight is here with a pair  of personalities and a very cool suit  the first episode is full of twists and  turns but it's the ending that reveals  the most about moon knight and his foes  warning spoilers ahead  steven grant is a man tormented by a  situation that he doesn't fully  understand and he tries to control his  tendency to wander around while he's  unconscious with a number of diy tricks  it's clear that this has been going on  for a long time and moonlight episode 1  is when everything finally changes as  the first episode nears its end stephen  gets to peek behind the veil when he  discovers physical evidence of another  personality's existence tucked away in a  hidey hole in his apartment a cell phone  he discovers is a particularly important  find because it introduces viewers to  multiple potentially important  characters shortly after discovering the  old phone stephen gets a call on the  other end an unfamiliar woman named  layla has been trying to reach a man  named mark for what appears to be weeks  who do you think i am what do you mean  who what's wrong with you mark  layla might very well turn out to be the  mcu version of mark's romantic interest  in the comics marlene the other name in  the miss calls list duchamp is also very  interesting duchamp is almost certainly  frenchy duchamp mark's old mercenary  friend and ally in the comics it remains  to be seen whether his name is a simple  easter egg or a tease of the character's  on-screen debut still the fact that he  exists in the mcu implies that mark and  frenchie's old mercenary boss and moon  knight arguably greatest enemy rattle  buschmann also lurks somewhere in the  world while mark's formidable nemesis  seems like the kind of character the mcu  might want to save for moonlight season  2 or even a movie fans will no doubt  welcome this low-key confirmation that  bushman might make an appearance at some  point down the line  in the comics moon knight's various  personalities often converse with each  other and konju is fond of making  physical appearances in all of his  bird's girl-headed glory it's a pretty  wild concept for a live-action show and  indeed moon knight episode 1 makes it  clear that the series intends to keep  such interactions at a relatively muted  voices in his head level during the  mid-episode chase scene f murray  abraham's kanchu establishes himself as  a pestering presence that mostly uses  his booming voice to express  exasperation over stephen's lack of  mercenary prowess  the idiot's in control  while the discovery of mark's phone  finally clues stephen into the fact that  he shares his body with another identity  it also spirals his life further into  disarray his existence is suddenly all  about mark talking to him through  mirrors and consume manifesting in front  of him in dramatic horror movie fashion  though these experiences are obviously  no fun for steven the mirror dialogue is  an effective visual technique that  translates the identity's comic book  conversations to the live-action medium  meanwhile khanshu's ominous stalking  hallway appearance is that complete odds  with the almost flipping way the  characters disembodied voice converses  with steven earlier in the episode this  gives the viewer a glimpse of the  character's unpredictable otherworldly  nature as well as the moon god's  tendency to ignore the mental well-being  of its avatar  it becomes clear very quickly that moon  knight's primary nemesis arthur harrow  is more than a small time cult leader  with a penchant for filling his shoes  with ground glass not only does the  villain have the powers of ahmet and  egyptian goddess of justice but the cult  he leads has also infiltrated all levels  of society this is revealed when harrow  confronts stephen and the british museum  so you really do work here oh god i'd  assumed stephen grant was an alias i'll  imagine my surprise to find you here  yet the security guard whom stephen  knows and who's clearly been at the  museum for a while is a full member of  team ahmet this fact is confirmed when  the guard reveals a scale tattoo on his  arm similar to the one harrow possesses  it means that the guard has been at the  museum for reasons that have nothing to  do with stephen which in turn implies  one of two things either harrow place a  guard there for an entirely unrelated  purpose or his call are simply so  formidable that he has followers  everywhere considering the museum's vast  egyptology department with a vast  collection of ahmed themed artifacts the  placement of the guard doesn't seem  accidental and when harrow proceeds to  outright state that his plans for the  world will cause millions of deaths it  becomes clear that he's a global threat  while it remains to be seen just how  widespread the cult of ahmed is this  version of arthur harrow is definitely a  far more powerful and dangerous man than  the mad doctor from the comics as  harrow's summoned jackal creature corner  stephen in the museum bathroom and  starts punching his way through the  heavy doors it's clear that the beast's  strength matches its supernatural  creepiness fortunately a panicked mirror  conversation between stephen and mark  convinces the timid brit to yield  control of their shared body just as the  creature burst through the doors stephen  stephen i could save us  i can't have you fighting me this time  what follows is yet another scene  straight out of a horror movie at least  for the jackal moon knight completely  and utterly overwhelms and destroys the  beast ignoring its feeble attempts to  defend itself and taking it down with a  few brutal attacks this short scene ends  the episode with a punch literally and  while it gives viewers the first good  look at the awesome moonlight costume it  also offers a sample of something even  more interesting the character's powers  moon knight's strength is all over the  place in the comics to put it mildly  sometimes he's just a well-trained guy  with some gadgets and kevlar at the  times he commands a vast array of super  powers that allow him to take down the  avengers all by himself as such it's  interesting to see where on the sliding  scale the mcu character lands based on  the fact that he effortlessly defeats  the superpowered jackal creature it's  clear that he's no weakling there's no  telling what he can do when he unleashes  his weapons and really lets loose but we  have a sneaking suspicion that future  episodes of moon knight will shed plenty  of light on his true power level  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  moon night are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

